### PRD & Screenshot Test Case Generator — REST Client requests
### Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client),
### then click "Send Request" above any line starting with ###.
### Companion to ../README.md — same 10 exercises as the Postman collection and the
### curl cheatsheet, as plain, version-controlled text instead of an app you open.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Exercise 0: health check — static UI loads
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### Exercise 7: list history (run this before "get history item" below,
### then copy an id from the response into the request underneath it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/history

### Exercise 8: get one history item by id — replace 37 with a real id from above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/history/37

### Exercise 9: get a history item that doesn't exist (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/history/999999999

### Exercise 2: analyze PRD with no body/Content-Type at all.
### Expect 415, not 400 — consumes="multipart/form-data" rejects a non-multipart
### request before the controller method ever runs. (A real discrepancy with
### ApiSmokeTest.analyzePrd_withNoFile_returns400(), which currently asserts 400
### for this same case.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prd/analyze

### Exercise 3: analyze PRD with a real, 0-byte file (expect 400, "No file was
### uploaded" — Spring's MultipartFile.isEmpty() is true for 0 bytes, so this
### hits the SAME branch as sending no file at all, not text extraction)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prd/analyze
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="empty.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

------boundary--

### Exercise 4: analyze PRD with a 1-byte whitespace-only file (expect 400,
### "No extractable text was found" — this is the request that actually reaches
### the text-extraction branch, distinct from the 0-byte case above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prd/analyze
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="blank.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ../fixtures/blank.txt
------boundary--

### Exercise 1: analyze PRD — happy path (real Gemini call, can take ~1 min)
### The `< ./path` syntax below tells REST Client to read the file's bytes as the body part.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/prd/analyze
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="password-reset-prd.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ../../samples/password-reset-prd.md
------boundary--

### Exercise 6: analyze screenshot with a non-image file (expect 400 — the
### controller checks the multipart part's Content-Type, not the extension)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/screenshot/analyze
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----boundary

------boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="password-reset-prd.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ../../samples/password-reset-prd.md
------boundary--

